close_reason: Append-only history repair shipped in PR #1762
contract_change:
  api: "pm history-repair --append-only, HistoryRepairCommandOptions.appendOnly, HistoryRepairResult.bridge, HistoryEntry.bridge and replay_inexact, verifyHistoryChainWithVersion, ReanchorHistoryOptions.callerMarksBridgeCoverage, ReanchorResult.entriesResealed and HistoryMergeStrategy"
  before: "The only repair for a broken history chain re-anchored every recorded entry after the break, and HistoryMergeStrategy had four members"
  after: "--append-only (SDK and MCP appendOnly) appends one sealed history_repair record whose bridge names each break and leaves every earlier line byte-identical. verifyHistoryChainWithVersion accepts a break only when the next bridge names it and reports bridged_segments. A rewrite that dissolves a bridge marks the covered versions with the sealed replay_inexact field, and restore and get --at refuse them with history_version_unreconstructable. The history merge driver adds the equivalent_bridges strategy, and pm health names --append-only as the remedy for history_drift_chain_mismatch"
  migrate: "Add a case for equivalent_bridges to exhaustive switches over HistoryMergeStrategy; raw history readers should ignore the optional bridge and replay_inexact fields or verify through verifyHistoryChainWithVersion, and treat history_version_unreconstructable as a refused version"
escape_class: production_defect
gate_evidence:
  disposition: gate_added
  owner: pm-gh1715
  gate_id: history-bridge-verification
  negative_control: "tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts verifies a stream with a bridge whose segment digest, named breaks, link, epoch, anchors or after-hash were altered and asserts each typed verification failure (bridge_invalid, bridge_unnamed_break, bridge_names_absent_break, bridge_segment_mismatch, bridge_link_mismatch, bridge_epoch_mismatch, bridge_after_hash_mismatch, record_incomplete, bridge_without_break). It also asserts that restore refuses every covered version with history_version_unreconstructable before and after redaction, normalization, compaction and merge unions dissolve the bridge."
  local_checks[3]: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/integration/lifecycle/history-bridge.integration.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/history/append-only-repair.spec.ts tests/unit/core/history/history-bridge.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/merge/history-bridge-merge.spec.ts,node scripts/release/static-quality-gate.mts,node scripts/sdk-surface-snapshot.mjs --check
  hosted_checks[2]: CI / Gates (static),CI / Gates (coverage)
